Patch-Source: https://github.com/NoiseByNorthwest/php-spx/pull/343

Give every test that writes a profiling report its own spx.data_dir.

Six tests write full reports into the shared, hardcoded default data dir
/tmp/spx (src/php_spx.c:113 - "spx.data_dir", "/tmp/spx", PHP_INI_SYSTEM), and
two of them wipe that whole directory in their --CLEAN-- section:

    tests/spx_ini_params_profiling_enabled.phpt:18: exec("rm -rf /tmp/spx");
    tests/spx_ini_params_not_overridden.phpt:28:    exec("rm -rf /tmp/spx");

while tests/spx_custom_metadata.phpt reads its own reports back with
file_get_contents('/tmp/spx/' . $key . '.json').

Since php-src 1d2ea5ce22c ("Run tests in parallel by default", GH-22939, first
released in php-8.6.0beta1) run-tests.php spawns min(nproc, 10) workers by
default, so the readers race the wipers and spx_custom_metadata.phpt fails with
"file_get_contents(): Failed to open stream: No such file or directory".
On an 8-core builder this reproduced in 15 out of 15 parallel runs.

spx.data_dir is PHP_INI_SYSTEM and is therefore settable per test from --INI--,
exactly the way tests/spx_ui_report_access.phpt already does it. Point each
report-producing test at its own {PWD}/data_dir_<test> and remove only that
directory in --CLEAN--, so no test can ever clobber another's reports, nothing
is left behind in /tmp, and the suite stays fully parallel.

Note --CLEAN-- scripts are executed with the *global* ini settings, not the
test's --INI-- section, so the clean-up path is spelled out with __DIR__ rather
than read back via ini_get().

--- a/tests/spx_auto_start_005.phpt
+++ b/tests/spx_auto_start_005.phpt
@@ -1,5 +1,7 @@
 --TEST--
 Auto start disabled, full report & span report keys printed
+--INI--
+spx.data_dir="{PWD}/data_dir_auto_start_005"
 --ENV--
 return <<<END
 SPX_ENABLED=1
@@ -28,4 +30,10 @@
 --EXPECTF--
 spx-full-%s
 spx-full-%s
-spx-full-%s
\ No newline at end of file
+spx-full-%s
+--CLEAN--
+<?php
+
+exec("rm -rf " . escapeshellarg(__DIR__ . "/data_dir_auto_start_005"));
+
+?>
--- a/tests/spx_auto_start_007.phpt
+++ b/tests/spx_auto_start_007.phpt
@@ -3,6 +3,7 @@
 --CGI--
 --INI--
 spx.debug=1
+spx.data_dir="{PWD}/data_dir_auto_start_007"
 spx.http_enabled=1
 spx.http_key="dev"
 spx.http_ip_whitelist="127.0.0.1"
@@ -33,4 +34,10 @@
 --EXPECTF--
 spx-full-%s
 spx-full-%s
-spx-full-%s
\ No newline at end of file
+spx-full-%s
+--CLEAN--
+<?php
+
+exec("rm -rf " . escapeshellarg(__DIR__ . "/data_dir_auto_start_007"));
+
+?>
--- a/tests/spx_custom_metadata.phpt
+++ b/tests/spx_custom_metadata.phpt
@@ -2,6 +2,7 @@
 Custom metadata
 --INI--
 log_errors=on
+spx.data_dir="{PWD}/data_dir_custom_metadata"
 --ENV--
 return <<<END
 SPX_ENABLED=1
@@ -32,7 +33,7 @@
     foo();
 
     $key = spx_profiler_stop();
-    echo file_get_contents('/tmp/spx/' . $key . '.json');
+    echo file_get_contents(__DIR__ . '/data_dir_custom_metadata/' . $key . '.json');
 }
 
 ?>
@@ -154,4 +155,10 @@
     "wt"
     ,"zm"
   ]
-}
\ No newline at end of file
+}
+--CLEAN--
+<?php
+
+exec("rm -rf " . escapeshellarg(__DIR__ . "/data_dir_custom_metadata"));
+
+?>
